:: Day4Start [nobr]
<div class="title-screen">
<div class="th">दूसरी चमड़ी</div>
<div class="te">Day 4   Doosri Chamdi · Second Skin</div>

<p class="lede">The alarm at 4:15 wasn't a surprise this time. You lay awake for most of the hour before it anyway. Second swap. Same circle, same thread, same 1,500-year-old rock   and the two of you have done this once, which turns out to change everything and nothing.</p>

<p class="lede">Arjun has to get out of the PG past a sleeping Rohit and a door that has never once opened quietly. Kavya walks out of the hostel on the seven-day pooja cover she planted yesterday   Ramesh has already told himself the story. Swap at 5:30, twelve hours, back at 5:30 sharp.</p>

<p class="lede">You play both threads. Kavya mentioned a countdown on the swap this morning   day 22 of a cycle, six days of buffer   and then said "not today, focus on today." So: today.</p>

<div class="start-btn">
<<link "4:25 AM   move">><<goto "Hub">><</link>>
</div>
</div>


:: day4_temple_wait
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, pre-dawn">>
You sit on the cold steps. You know this sky now   the way it doesn't lighten so much as thin, paper against a lamp.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya checks the kumkum tin, the thread, the printed sheet, twice, in the same order as yesterday. <div class="dialogue">"You're three minutes late again. Your body's clock runs behind, I've decided that's a hardware fault, not a you fault."</div>
<<else>>Arjun's knee is going, but slower than yesterday. He catches you looking and stops it himself. "Second time," he says. "It's still real. I checked."<</if>>

<<hubreturn "Sit in the circle">>


:: day4_temple_wait_back
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, waiting">>
You're back in the courtyard but the circle won't do anything yet   it needs both of you here and both of your days actually finished.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You sit on the warm evening stone in Kavya's body, re-pinning the dupatta out of habit, watching the road. Across the city there's still a version of your own face with coding left to do.

<div class="thought arjun">Switch over. Get Kavya's day closed   the bonus problem   and bring her here.</div>
<<else>>You sit on the steps in Arjun's body, legs sprawled the way his want to. No maroon salwar on the path yet. Arjun still has the afternoon with Meera to finish over there.

<div class="thought kavya">Switch over. Let him have his hours. Then this works.</div>
<</if>>

<<hubreturn>>


:: day4_swap
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The swap   again</span>
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "the kumkum circle, second time">>
<<if $pov is "arjun">>She's on the steps in the pre-dawn grey when the Pulsar's headlight sweeps the courtyard. Salwar, dupatta wound tight, the Redmi lighting her face from below.

"You're three minutes late."

"The door squeaked."

<div class="dialogue">"I heard about the door. Through the text you didn't answer because you were being a spy in your own PG."</div>

You zip the Pulsar key into the jacket pocket and pat it once   the handover's a routine now.
<<else>>Arjun rolls in on the Pulsar three minutes after you'd have liked. He kills the engine, and before the circle he zips the key into the jacket pocket and pats it, the same motion as yesterday.

<div class="dialogue">"You're three minutes late."</div>

"The door squeaked."

<div class="dialogue">"I heard about the door."</div>
<</if>>

You sit cross-legged inside the kumkum circle, knees almost touching. The thread goes around both right wrists. <<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya<<else>>You<</if>> loop it taut.

<<if $pov is "kavya">>Then the briefing, delivered clinical, the medical student reporting on the body she's lending out.

<div class="dialogue">"My left bra strap is dying. Safety-pin it to the kameez from inside   I showed you. And Arjun."</div> You hold his gaze until it's steady. <div class="dialogue">"My body got its period 3 weeks ago. Day 22 of the cycle. You have about six days before the next one. When it's closer I'll walk you through the whole thing   pads, cramps, the logistics. For today you're safe. Just   know the countdown is running."</div>

His face   your face   goes the pale that happens when blood heads for fight-or-flight. "Period. As in blood, cramps   "

"As in NOT today. Six days. Focus on today."
<<else>>Then Kavya, clinical, briefing you on the body she's handing over:

<div class="dialogue">"Left bra strap's dying   safety-pin it to the kameez from inside, the way I showed you. And one more thing."</div> She waits until you're looking at her properly. <div class="dialogue">"My body had its period 3 weeks ago. Day 22. You've got about six days of buffer before the next one. When it's close I'll brief you properly   pads, cramps, all of it. Today you're clear. Just know it's coming."</div>

The word arrives in your chest like a cold front. "Period. As in   "

<div class="dialogue">"As in not today. Six days. Focus on today."</div>

Six days of buffer between you and the single most fundamentally female experience you cannot currently imagine. A background process starts up in the back of your mind, counting down.
<</if>>

The chant begins   the same printed sheet, Kavya leading, the other half a beat behind and clicked back on line. Second time through, the words come easier. The dark around the lamp leans in the same way.

Count 50   heartbeat. Count 80   the thread warms. Count 90   the headache at light speed.

Count 97   <b>THE WRENCH.</b> You brace for it this time, jumping into cold water the second time. It's still awful   still being hauled through a keyhole backwards   but the recovery is faster. Ten seconds of black, not thirty.

Black.
</div>
\
<<run setup.setBody("arjun", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.setBody("kavya", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.flag("swap_complete")>>\
<<run setup.doSwap()>>\
<<set $swapActive to true>>\
<<run setup.removeItem("bike_keys", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.addItem("bike_keys", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.removeItem("redmi_phone", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.addItem("redmi_phone", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 2, "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.stat("rel_kavya_arjun", 2, "kavya")>>\
<<run $time.arjun = 330>>\
<<run $time.kavya = 330>>\
<<run $loc.arjun = "hostel_walk_d4">>\
<<run $loc.kavya = "pulsar_ride_d4">>\
<<set $mood.arjun to "settled into the wrong side of the mirror">>\
<<set $mood.kavya to "back in the good body">>

<div class="continue-nav"><<link "Sit up. Faster this time.">><<goto "day4_briefing">><</link>></div>


:: day4_briefing
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The handover   short version</span>
<<img "day3_briefing.png" "two strangers wearing familiar faces, take two">>
Colour bleeds back. You're breathing hard in the circle and three feet away your own face is looking at you with an expression you've now seen twice.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>"It's you again," you say, in Kavya's voice. "That's my face. On you." You turn Kavya's small ringed hand over and it obeys. "Yesterday I couldn't believe it. Today I just   know it. That's worse, somehow. It's a thing that happens to us now."

<div class="dialogue">"That's the correct amount of alarm. Keep it. Priya has a 7 AM yoga class   she'll be out when you reach. Meera's waiting."</div>
<<else>>Arjun does the hand-check   turns your hands over, presses them to his (your) face, hair, throat   but it's five seconds this time, not five minutes.

<div class="dialogue">"Second time. That's my face on you and I'm not coming apart about it, which is somehow more disturbing."</div>

"That's the right amount of disturbed," you tell him, in your own lower voice. "Keep it. Priya's got 7 AM yoga   she'll be gone when you get there. Meera's up."
<</if>>

The notes exchange is quick   yesterday's pages, updated in the margins. Ramesh at the gate (the pooja cover holds all week). Rohit's the sensor. Don't be brilliant in Krishnan's class. Pooja texts fast, three words or nothing. The one hard rule doesn't need saying again, but <<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya says it anyway, one line: "You do not touch my body. Same as yesterday. Yes?"

"Yes. Nothing it doesn't need. Go."
<<else>>you say it anyway, one line: "You do not touch my body. Same terms. Yes?"

<div class="dialogue">"Yes. Nothing it doesn't need. Go."</div>
<</if>>

<<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya swings onto the Pulsar, stalls it once out of muscle memory, catches it on the second try, and rides into the Pune dawn wearing your face. "Back here, 5:30 sharp," she calls over the engine. "Clean window. Don't lose my body."
<<else>>You swing onto the Pulsar, stall it once, catch it on the second, and ride out. "Back here, 5:30 sharp," you call over your shoulder in his voice. "Don't lose my body."
<</if>>

You touch your borrowed face once and walk out in opposite directions. Twelve hours.
</div>
\
<<run setup.flag("day4_briefed")>>\
<<run setup.discover("the second swap   faster, quieter, more frightening for being ordinary", $pov)>>
<div class="continue-nav"><<link "Open your eyes on the day">><<goto "Hub">><</link>></div>


:: EV_a4_priya_out
Priya gathers her laptop and two pathology textbooks at 12:45 and heads for the library, chasing the AC. The door closes. The lock engages.

The room is yours. Meera's already sitting up straighter.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a4_checkin_arjun
<div class="alert-popup swap" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Arjun (VIT, corridor)</div>

You call. He picks up in your own voice.

<div class="dialogue">"Red-Black trees. Krishnan. Insertion cases. I answered ONE question. ONE. 'Uncle node's colour, sir.' Then I sat on my hands for forty minutes. It's like being a sprinter made to walk."</div>

"Good restraint."

<div class="dialogue">"Good restraint has a cost. How's my body?"</div>

"The bra was first try today. Twenty seconds, no Meera."

A beat. Then, quietly, in your voice: <div class="dialogue">"I'm proud of you."</div>

"I'm proud of me too. Also I noticed something in the bathroom this time. Your body's always   on. Between the legs. Always sensing. Mine's a thing I carry; yours is a thing that lives."

<div class="dialogue">"Twenty-one years of continuous monitoring. You're welcome. The erection situation   we're not doing that on the phone."</div>

"Deferred to the temple. Bring vocabulary."

<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 3, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a4_swapback_reminder_a
The Redmi buzzes. Kavya: //Temple. 5:30   twelve hours to the minute. Last clean window for the hostel. I want my hands back and you want yours.//

You look at Kavya's hands. The silver ring. The short shaped nails you've stopped fumbling with. A small flicker of something like loss, again.

<<hubreturn>>


