:: EV_a4_rohit_lab
Rohit stands, stretches, announces "Mechanical lab, four hours, kill me" as if his own timetable had personally wronged him, and leaves. The door closes. His footsteps recede.

The room is yours. The laptop is yours. Until five.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a4_swapback_reminder_k
Arjun's phone buzzes. Meera, via the Samsung: //5:30. Pataleshwar. Twelve hours exactly, last clean hour for Kavya's hostel. He needs his body and you need yours. And Kavya   thank you. For the classes. For treating my world like it matters.//

You look at the clock on the borrowed screen. The keyboard under your hands. Soon this stops.

<<hubreturn>>


:: day4_swapback
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The swap-back</span>
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, golden hour">>
The circle again, in the flat gold light of half past five, the courtyard empty in the lull before evening aarti. The thread. The mantra in reverse. The wrench   braced for, endured, over.

Black. White. Colours resolving.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You open your eyes and the first thing is your cock, right there, the familiar weight. Flat chest. Full lungs. Taller   the temple walls back at eye level.

Then the loss, immediate and sharp: the sensitivity is gone. You touch your own arm and it's just skin on skin. No ripples, no stone-in-water, no conversation. Meera's hug replays in your head and your body stores it flat now   a photograph, where twelve hours ago it was a room you could stand inside.

<div class="dialogue">"How was VIT?"</div>

"Heaven. How was my body?" Kavya's patting herself down   face, chest, hips, the property audit.

"Complicated."

<div class="dialogue">"...did you cry?"</div>

"...maybe."

<div class="dialogue">"Day 2 in my body and you're already more emotional than I am. Sit. Full debrief."</div>
<<else>>You open your eyes and your breasts are back   two familiar masses settling onto the ribcage, the Clovia underwire that Arjun hooked this morning still holding, clamping down. Twelve hours flat and free, and the whole production returns. The world drops. You're small again. And between your legs, the absence where a warm ridiculous weight used to be   not wrong, just newly noticeable.

"Your laptop is beautiful," you tell Arjun, and the tears come, Kavya's zero-latency system firing. "I solved the bonus problem. Two submissions, one fake bug. It looked exactly like learning." You wipe your face with a hand that's yours again. "Sit. Full debrief. Rule seven."

<div class="dialogue">"Also your Pulsar corners better when I ride it. I sit straighter than you do."</div>
<</if>>

You sit on the cooling stone and do the thing the rules demand.

<<if $pov is "kavya">>You go first.<<else>>Kavya goes first.<</if>>

<div class="dialogue">"CS: I attended, I understood every word, I answered exactly one question at the right IQ. Then I solved Krishnan's deletion edge case on real hardware   the double-red violation   and buried a deliberate mistake in version one so the trail reads try, fail, learn. Nikhil's got a copy. Rohit's on the 'since when do you know this' setting; I gave him the Meera-wake-up story and he half-bought it again."</div>

<div class="dialogue">"Raju's chai supplier collapsed   I Googled him three wholesalers, he closed a deal at the counter, I have a month of free chai in your name. Your sister built a calculator and then googled 'error handling.' Aai asked if computers bring money. Pooja is going to be a programmer, Arjun, and she doesn't know it yet."</div>

Then <<if $pov is "arjun">>your<<else>>Arjun's<</if>> turn.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You give her the shape of Meera   the door bolted, two hours, Meera's arms around a smaller frame with the geometry inverted, her hand coming to rest on the outer curve of a breast that isn't hers, through the kameez, and stopping there. The nipple's autonomous answer. The crying. Your hands where they belonged and nowhere else. She nods once, approving, doesn't ask for the rest.

Then the survival log: the bra solo in twenty seconds; the second pee and what the tissue does during the wipe; the anatomy hall on Meera's cough protocol, Dr. Sharma complimenting "Kavya's" technique that was entirely Meera's; Sneha clocking the handwriting again; Priya clocking the phone in the wrong place. Crying maybe three times, down from six.

<div class="dialogue">"Three. Improvement."</div>

"Your tear ducts still have no latency. I've just stopped fighting them."
<<else>>Arjun gives you the shape of Meera   bolted door, two hours, the inversion of every embrace you've shared, her hand on the outer curve of your breast through the kameez and no further. What your body does near Meera that his doesn't. His hands where they belonged.

Then the survival log: bra solo, twenty seconds; the second pee and the tissue-awareness thing; anatomy on Meera's cough protocol; Sneha on the handwriting; Priya on the phone position. Three cries, down from six.

<div class="dialogue">"Three. That's progress."</div>

"Your tear ducts still have no latency. I've stopped fighting them."
<</if>>

You both laugh, real, in your own voices, off 1,500-year-old stone.

Then Kavya, practical, because that's her at rest.

<div class="dialogue">"Same again tomorrow. 5 AM, this circle. Krishnan's symposium is still hanging, ICPC's Saturday, Meera's expecting you, and the period countdown is at five days now   which we deal with when it's four. Alarm at 4:15. Don't sleep well."</div>

<<if $pov is "arjun">>"Every day," you say, before the arithmetic finishes.<<else>>"Every day," Arjun says, too fast, the way he says yes to anything with Meera in it.<</if>>

The second skin is fitting. That's the part that should frighten you more than the wrench does.
</div>\
