:: day4_gohome
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The ride home</span>
<<if $pov is "arjun">>You wheel the Pulsar out of the temple lot   your bike, your hands, your weight over the tank   and ride down into Pune's evening. Katraj is forty minutes of horns and diesel and a body that does exactly what you tell it. Rohit's still out. The PG room is dark and yours and smells of Axe and stale Maggi, and it looks fine. It looks good.

Across the city, Kavya signs back into the B.J. hostel in her own round hand   //K. Iyer, in, 18:05, temple//   nods at Ramesh, climbs to 304, where Meera is holding a book she isn't reading.
<<else>>You sign back into the hostel yourself   //K. Iyer, in, 18:05, temple//, your own round hand, nothing to forge   nod at Ramesh, climb to 304. Meera looks up from a book she isn't reading. Priya isn't. You're home, in your own skin.

Across the city, Arjun rides the Pulsar back to Katraj in his own body, in a helmet that fits, toward a dark PG room that smells of Axe and stale Maggi.
<</if>>

You each carry the same thing home: a second day that happened, and a 4:15 alarm.
</div>\
<<run setup.flag("arjun_home_d4")>>\
<<run setup.flag("kavya_home_d4")>>\
